# Mutants of the behaviour scripts' abstract machine and the script system (at/smallvm: src/at/AtSmallVm.cpp, src/at/AtSmallCScripts.cpp,
# src/at/AtSmallCScriptOwner.cpp). Each text occurs exactly once in its file. Run by tests/oracle/oracle_smallvm.cpp.
#
# Dropped as equivalent, each with its reason:
#  * Exec resuming from the machine's data address instead of the saved one: nothing in the executable changes a script's m_base while a call is
#    suspended (a copy made by CallPublic is destroyed with its state), so the saved data address always equals m_base + dat.
#  * FILL doing nothing below 1 byte instead of below 4: for 1 to 3 bytes both write nothing and leave the operand global as the operand.
#  * Reset leaving the flags: Reset is only ever followed by the destructor or the end of CallPublic's local copy; nothing reads the flags after it.
#  * Cancel testing flag 8 instead of flag 2: through every member that writes them (StartScript, Run, CallPublic, Activate, Cancel) the two are set and
#    cleared together, so they are equal wherever Cancel can look.
V = "AtSmallVm.cpp"
C = "AtSmallCScripts.cpp"
O = "AtSmallCScriptOwner.cpp"

